    "durationMs": 1443039,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. The URL shortener is built with Spring Boot 3.4.5, Spring Data JPA, PostgreSQL, and Flyway:\n\n- **Endpoints**: POST /links (201, 409 duplicate, 422 validation), GET /links/{code} (200/404), GET /r/{code} (302 with atomic click increment), GET /links (creation-ordered items/total) — all error responses carry an `error` field\n- **Persistence**: DATABASE_URL parsed at startup into JDBC settings (no hard-coded credentials), Flyway migration `V1__links.sql`, data and click counts verified to survive restart\n- **start.sh**: executable, applies pending migrations at boot then serves in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000; all dependencies installed and the jar prebuilt (`mvn -DskipTests package`)\n- **README**: documents how to start the server\n\nI ran the full requirement matrix (including boundary codes, malformed bodies, redirects, and a restart test) — everything passes, test rows were removed, and port 8000 is free for the grading run."
  }
